+#### `requestUserApproval`
+
+Use `requestUserApproval` when another extension owns a deterministic policy but needs the permission system's user-prompt and direct-child forwarding transport.
+The caller supplies two to eight choices with stable IDs and unique labels; the result returns the selected ID.
+The permission system does not interpret the choice, persist a grant, or change its own policy.
+Invalid requests reject, while unavailable UI, cancellation, timeout, and malformed forwarded responses fail closed with `choiceId: null`.
+
+```typescript
+const result = await permissions.requestUserApproval({
+  requestId: toolCallId,
+  title: "Sandbox permission",
+  message: "Allow read access to /outside/input?",
+  source: "tool_call",
+  surface: "read",
+  value: "/outside/input",
+  choices: [
+    { id: "once", label: "Allow once" },
+    { id: "always", label: "Always allow in this workspace" },
+    { id: "deny", label: "No" },
+  ],
+  signal,
+});
+
+if (result.choiceId === "always") {
+  saveWorkspaceGrant();
+}
+```
+
+A choice may set `requestReason: true` to ask for a short note after selection; the note returns as `result.reason`.
+The caller may pass `reasonTitle` and `reasonPlaceholder` to label that input.
+The request message and choices cross a private owner-only file transport for process-based direct children, so do not include secrets that the parent UI does not need.
+Nested process children remain limited by the same direct-parent routing rule described in [Subagent Integration](subagent-integration.md).
+
 #### `registerToolInputFormatter`
 
 Register a custom preview formatter for a specific tool name.
